# ==== T-FMT-D (R41) fill-pack matrix — LIST KIND = GROUPED-IMPORT name list.
#
# SUBJECT: this fixture asserts `gg fmt` OUTPUT (byte-for-byte, in
# `fmt_fill_pack_import_group_kind`) — a bulk `gg fmt` sweep MUST EXCLUDE it.
#
# Emit site: the `ImportStmt::Grouped` arm of `format_import` ->
# `emit_delimited_texts("{", "}", ..)` -> `doc::surround_fill`.
#
# This kind used to be the ONE that called `emit_delimited_texts` DIRECTLY, as
# the single declared carve-out from the interior-comment gate. The reason was
# the alphabetical name SORT: emitted order was not source order, and the
# comment cursor is forward-only, so per-element interleaving would have
# flushed a later name's comment against an earlier one. The 2026-08-16 canon
# removed the sort (names keep the AUTHOR's order), the reason went with it,
# and the group now routes through `emit_delimited_list` like every other list
# — which is why a comment inside a grouped import now stays inside it
# (`fmt_import_group_interior_comment_stays_inside`). `EXPECTED_UNGATED_TEXTS`
# is 0 and `EXPECTED_DELIMITED_LIST_SITES` is 10.
#
# ⚠ The names below are in AUTHOR order, NOT alphabetical. That is the point:
# an alphabetised expectation here is a regression, not a tidy-up.
#
# Axis cell claim (Core #12 — `list kind x fit` for the IMPORT-GROUP kind ONLY):
#   std.io       fits-flat          one line, no trailing comma
#   std.collect  needs-fill         greedy packing at the block continuation indent
#   std.math     single-over-width  the one name does not fit on the open line, so it
#                                    breaks to the continuation indent, alone
#
# The EMPTY cell has no spelling: `import a.{}` is a parse error.
#
# The `from std.text import ..` line below is the deliberately NON-converted
# sibling: `ImportStmt::From` never wraps at all, because a bare name on a fresh
# line re-parses as a new statement in indentation-based syntax. It must stay on
# ONE line however long it gets — that is what this row pins.
#
# RED source per row: the grouped `std.collections` / `std.math` rows are TRUE
# pre-fix REDs (one name per line with a trailing comma and a bare `}`). The
# `std.io` row and the `from` row are invariant — break-and-restore them by
# lowering `doc::MAX_WIDTH` (the `from` row must NOT move even then).
import std.io.{Alpha, Beta, Gamma}
import std.collections.{Alpha, Beta, Gamma, Delta, Epsilon, Zeta, Eta, Theta, Iota, Kappa, Lambda, Mu, Nu, Xi, Omicron, Pi, Rho}
import std.math.{ASingleImportedNameWhoseRenderedWidthAloneExceedsTheEntireLineWidthBudgetOfTheGorgetCanonicalSourceFormatter}
from std.text import Aaaaaaaaaa, Bbbbbbbbbb, Cccccccccc, Dddddddddd, Eeeeeeeeee, Ffffffffff, Gggggggggg, Hhhhhhhhhh

void iu():
    print(1)
